ptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanVS/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanVS/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanVS/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanVS/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":12,"created_at":"2016-02-26T14:18:50Z","updated_at":"2018-02-06T23:24:53Z","closed_at":"2016-03-22T19:26:25Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"I am developing React Native application and I am keeping the code inside `node_modules/mylibrary`. The reason why I keep it there is to avoid relative paths between modules in my library and that's the recommended way to do that according to [this](https://github.com/substack/browserify-handbook#node_modules). I would use symlinks if it wasn't for [this](https://github.com/facebook/react-native/issues/637).\n\nI would therefore like to lint code in `node_modules/mylibrary`. Because `node_modules` are by default ignored, I've tried adding the following line to `.eslintignore`, but it didn't help:\n\n```\n!node_modules/mylibrary/**/*.*\n```\n\n**What version of ESLint are you using?**\nv2.2.0\n\n**What configuration and parser (Espree, Babel-ESLint, etc.) are you using?**\nMy .eslintrc file looks like this:\n\n```\n{\n  \"extends\": [\"standard\"],\n  \"parser\": \"babel-eslint\"\n}\n```\n\n**What did you do? Please include the actual source code causing the issue.**\nI've created `node_modules/mylibrary/abc.js` with invalid content:\n\n```\nabc\n```\n\nBasically I am using atom editor and noticed that code is not linted. I confirmed it by calling three commands:\n\n```\n./node_modules/.bin/eslint --ignore-path .eslintignore ./node_modules/mylibrary\n./node_modules/.bin/eslint ./node_modules/mylibrary\n./node_modules/.bin/eslint --no-ignore ./node_modules/mylibrary\n```\n\n**What did you expect to happen?**\nI would expect the output to be the same for all three commands\n\n**What actually happened? Please include the actual, raw output from ESLint.**\nFirst two commands output nothing (no errors). Third one output:\n\n```\n/Users/tomkur/git/myproject/node_modules/mylibrary/abc.js\n  1:1  error  'abc' is not defined  no-undef\n\n✖ 1 problem (1 error, 0 warnings)\n```\n","closed_by":{"login":"nzakas","id":38546,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38546?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas","html_url":"https://github.com/nzakas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/5410/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/5410/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}